For every bin pair containing lists as in Lemma <a href="#seed:arrangement" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="seed:arrangement">7</a>, the midpoint gaps, including the fixed zero, satisfy $$\label{seed:gap-inequalities}
 g_{x,\mathrm{mid}}\le1-\frac{l-1}{N},\qquad
 g_{y,\mathrm{mid}}\ge1-\frac{l+2}{N}.$$

Every $V\in U(2)$ has a representation $$\label{completion:unitary-parameterization}
 V=e(\alpha)
 \begin{pmatrix}
 e(\beta)\cos(2\pi t)&e(\gamma)\sin(2\pi t)\\
 -e(-\gamma)\sin(2\pi t)&e(-\beta)\cos(2\pi t)
 \end{pmatrix},$$ with $0\le\alpha\le\tfrac12$, $0\le t\le\tfrac14$, and $0\le\beta,\gamma\le1$.

For the cell and displacement in <a href="#completion:unitary-cell" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="completion:unitary-cell">[completion:unitary-cell]</a>, $$\label{completion:unitary-taylor-bounds}
 \lVert V-U\rVert_F\le\sqrt6 h,\qquad
 \lVert V-U-dU[\theta]\rVert_F\le\frac{\sqrt{42}}2h^2.$$

For every cell midpoint $U\in U(2)$, $$\label{completion:L-definition}
 \lVert[C_0\ D]\rVert_{\rm op}\le
 L:=\max\left(\sqrt6,\;
 \lVert C_0\rVert_{\rm op}\sqrt{1+(A_0/m_B)^2}\right).$$

Either of the following is an upper bound for $\Delta\cdot u$: $$\begin{aligned}
 S_1={}&R_s\|(X^*\Delta)_s\|
          +h\|(X^*\Delta)_\theta\|_1
          +E_r\|\Delta_D\|
          +\|\Delta_D\|_\infty\mathtt{arc}^3/6, \label{phase:support-linear}\\
 S_2={}&R_s\|\Delta_s\|
          +\mathtt{weighted}
                  \left(\sum_{j\in\mathcal I_D}\Delta_j^2/m_j\right)^{1/2}.
 \label{phase:support-weighted}
\end{aligned}$$ Subscripts $s,D$ on a phase matrix mean restriction to $\mathcal I_s,\mathcal I_D$; subscripts on $X^*\Delta$ mean its nine seed and four angle coordinates.

For real linear maps $A,B$, vectors $\|s\|\leq r$, $\|v\|\leq q$, and $\beta>0$, the sum $As+Bv$ belongs to the ellipsoid $$\{G^{1/2}w:\|w\|\leq1\}
 \quad\hbox{whenever}\quad
 G\succeq(1+\beta)r^2AA^*+(1+1/\beta)q^2BB^*.$$

For every tangent box, $$\label{refine:corner-formula}
 \max_{\eta\in B(u,h)}\|\eta-\eta_q\|
 =\left(\sum_{a=1}^k(|u_a-\eta_{q,a}|+h)^2\right)^{1/2}.$$

For the indicated relation, the following necessary residual bound holds: $$\begin{aligned}
 \|q_{\mathcal O}+D_{\mathcal O}z\|
 &\le E_{\mathcal O}:=\pi r_e^2,
 &q_{\mathcal O}&=\frac{(\operatorname{Re}S,\operatorname{Im}S)^*}{2\pi},
 \label{exclude:orth-residual}\\
 |q_{\mathcal U}+D_{\mathcal U}z|
 &\le E_{\mathcal U}:=\pi r_e^2(1+|S|/6),
 &q_{\mathcal U}&=\frac{|S|^2/6-1}{4\pi}.
 \label{exclude:unbiased-residual}
\end{aligned}$$ Consequently the direct support tests $$\begin{aligned}
 \frac{|S|^2}{2\pi}
 &\le6r_e\|D_{\mathcal U}\|+E_{\mathcal O}|S|,
 \label{exclude:orth-support}\\
 |q_{\mathcal U}|&\le r_e\|D_{\mathcal U}\|+E_{\mathcal U}
 \label{exclude:unbiased-support}
\end{aligned}$$ are necessary as well.

